    "tier": 2,
    "description": "<p>A lean half-elf assassin who treats observation as the real job and violence as an optional conclusion. Finn works from prepared hides with suppressed weapons, custom toxins, and multiple escape routes, refusing any fight that becomes fair.</p>\n<section class=\"cybermancy-fast-play\"><h3>FAST PLAY</h3><p><strong><em>Opening:</em></strong> Shadow the team unseen until Finn has a clean assassination opportunity or another compelling reason to reveal himself.</p><p><strong><em>Default:</em></strong> From Hidden, use Precision Rifle to trigger Prepared Shot against exposed prey, then reset with Ghost Position rather than trade attacks.</p><p><strong><em>If Pressed:</em></strong> Use Exit Strategy when disengagement matters. Use Dead Drop when preparation can restore concealment, create escape, or disrupt pursuit.</p><p><strong><em>Fallback:</em></strong> Use Suppressed Pistol when close engagement is already advantageous; if the fight becomes fair, break contact.</p><p><strong><em>Remember:</em></strong> Relentless (2) permits a second spotlight but does not make it free. Any hit that marks HP triggers Finn's Compound.</p><p><strong><em>Goal:</em></strong> Make the PCs feel watched, suddenly endangered, then uncertain whether Finn is truly gone.</p></section>",
